  <img decoding="async" width="768" height="432" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/square-768x432-1.jpg" class="attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-post-image" alt="Square Building Bitcoin Hardware Wallet 'to Make Bitcoin Custody More Mainstream'" loading="lazy" style="float:left; margin:0 15px 15px 0;" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/square-768x432-1.jpg 768w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/square-300x169.jpg 300w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/square-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/square-696x385.jpg 696w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/square-1068x601.jpg 1068w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/square-747x420.jpg 747w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/square-190x107.jpg 190w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/square-380x214.jpg 380w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/square-760x428.jpg 760w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/square.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px" /></p> 
  
  <p>
    <strong>Jack Dorsey’s payments company, Square Inc., has confirmed that it is building a bitcoin hardware wallet and service with the aim to “make bitcoin custody more mainstream.”</strong>
  </p>
  
  <h2 style="text-align: center;">
    Square’s Bitcoin Hardware Wallet in the Works
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    Square Inc. is building a hardware wallet, Jesse Dorogusker, the company’s hardware lead, announced Thursday on Twitter. He tweeted:
  </p>
  
  <blockquote>
    <p>
      We have decided to build a hardware wallet and service to make bitcoin custody more mainstream. We’ll continue to ask and answer questions in the open.
    </p>
  </blockquote>
  
  <p>
    Square and Twitter CEO Jack Dorsey subsequently confirmed, tweeting: “We’re doing it.”
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <img decoding="async" srcset="https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/jacks-tweet-300x171.jpg 300w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/jacks-tweet-768x437.jpg 768w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/jacks-tweet-1024x583.jpg 1024w, https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/jacks-tweet.jpg 1326w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1326px) 100vw, 1326px" loading="lazy" class="size-full wp-image-473102 aligncenter" title="Jack Dorsey's Square Building Bitcoin Hardware Wallet to Make Crypto Custody More Mainstream" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/jacks-tweet.jpg" alt="Jack Dorsey's Square Building Bitcoin Hardware Wallet to Make Crypto Custody More Mainstream" width="1326" height="755" />
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Dorogusker explained: “Our next step is to build a small, cross-functional team, which will be led by Max Guise (welcome back). We will incubate this full-stack of tech, design, product, manufacturing, and supply chain with Thomas Templeton & Square’s hardware team to start with a strong foundation.” The hardware lead elaborated:
  </p>
  
  <blockquote>
    <p>
      We have a lot of questions and issues to reconcile and we’ll start with this product direction: bitcoin first, global distribution, multisig to achieve ‘assisted-self-custody,’ and prioritizing mobile use.
    </p>
  </blockquote>
  
  <p>
    <!-- growjs zone placement 31 -->
    
    <ins> <ins class="growjs-placement"></ins> </ins> <!-- end of growjs zone placement -->
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Dorsey first talked about his company considering building a hardware wallet on June 4.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    The Square and Twitter CEO wrote at the time: “If we do it, we would build it entirely in the open, from software to hardware design, and in collaboration with the community. We want to kick off this thinking the right way: by sharing some of our guiding principles.” He further opined:
  </p>
  
  <blockquote>
    <p>
      Bitcoin is for everyone. It’s important to us to build an inclusive product that brings a non-custodial solution to the global market.
    </p>
  </blockquote>
  
  <p>
    <em><strong>What do you think about Square building a bitcoin hardware wallet? Let us know in the comments section below.</strong></em>
  </p>
